00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.190 align:start position:0%
european union finance and economy  ministers will strive this week to forge  a common approach on new mechanisms to  preempt bank crises a key part of the  eu's ambitious banking union  the eco-finn council hopes to agree the  terms to establish a single  decision-making authority the so-called  single resolution mechanism and a single  fund to help banks under pressure  the aim is to help a struggling credit  institution or investment firm recover  from any shock in an orderly manner  preserving its operations and minimizing  the possibility of taxpayer losses  the authority and fund would help banks  to restructure in order to avoid  economic instability that could result  from liquidation  the rules must be agreed on by the  european parliament so eu nations would  like to move the package forward before  the assembly's current legislature ends  in may  the ministers will also seek to reach a  political agreement on rules governing  savings taxation  the aim is to update current legislation  dating from 2005 to take into account  all types of savings income and any  products that generate interest or  similar benefits  the proposal would also oblige  authorities to exchange information so  that interest payments made in one  nation to people from another eu state  are taxed under the laws of their  country of residence  the measures will help fight tax evasion  and tax fraud it's hoped that they can  be adopted by the end of the year
 

